2026-09-27T07:22:14.4614333Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4614515Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4614783Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4615041Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4615133Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4615327Z ================
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4615440Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4615605Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4615945Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4616152Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4616252Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4616507Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4616671Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4616796Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4617173Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4617504Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4618124Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4618622Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4618721Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4619125Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4619635Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4619902Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4620182Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4620567Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4620643Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4620826Z ========
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4620927Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4622171Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4623807Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4624027Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4624485Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4625263Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4625836Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4626376Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4698644Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4699166Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4699822Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4700320Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4700627Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4702807Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4704935Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4706162Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4707753Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4708138Z 
